# Super Heinz Bet Calculator 2026 - Calculate Your 7-Selection Returns
The super heinz calculator helps players in the United Kingdom calculate returns on 7-selection bets across Football and Horse Racing in 2026. This tool covers all 120 bet combinations from doubles through to the seven-fold accumulator.
## What Is a Super Heinz Bet?
A Super Heinz is a multiple bet consisting of 7 selections that creates 120 separate bets. The bet includes 21 doubles, 35 trebles, 35 four-fold accumulators, 21 five-fold accumulators, 7 six-fold accumulators, and 1 seven-fold accumulator. At least 2 selections must win for any return, though larger returns require more winning selections. This betting structure appeals to bettors who want coverage across multiple outcomes without requiring all selections to win.
The super heinz calculator football tool originated in the United Kingdom betting markets. Football matches represent the most common application, where bettors combine multiple match outcomes across different fixtures. Horse Racing events also feature prominently, particularly during festival periods when multiple races take place on the same day. Boxing matches occasionally appear in Super Heinz combinations, especially during major fight cards.
The 120-bet structure provides extensive coverage but requires careful stake management. Each individual bet carries the same stake amount, meaning a £1 Super Heinz costs £120 in total. The super heinz calculator determines potential returns by calculating each of the 120 combinations separately, then summing the winning bets based on actual results.
The breakdown of bet types shows the mathematical structure:
- 21 doubles cover every possible two-selection combination
- 35 trebles cover every three-selection combination
- 35 four-folds cover every four-selection combination
- 21 five-folds cover every five-selection combination
- 7 six-folds cover every six-selection combination
- 1 seven-fold combines all selections
Football bettors in the United Kingdom frequently use Super Heinz bets during weekends when multiple Premier League, Championship, and European fixtures run simultaneously. The bet type allows exposure to various outcomes while maintaining potential returns even when several selections lose. Horse Racing enthusiasts apply the same principle during meetings at venues across Britain, combining runners from different races into comprehensive betting structures.
The name derives from the Heinz bet (6 selections, 57 bets), with "Super" indicating the expanded seven-selection version. This betting format serves experienced bettors who understand accumulator mechanics and possess bankroll capacity for the 120-bet commitment.
